1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:03,210
By now, you should be aware

2
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:04,995
that effective team communication

3
00:00:04,995 --> 00:00:09,119
is necessary to help ensure a
successful project outcome.

4
00:00:09,119 --> 00:00:10,830
In this video, I'll share

5
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:13,230
more tips for communicating
with your team and

6
00:00:13,230 --> 00:00:15,720
introduce you to tools
that will help you and

7
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,674
your team communicate
even more effectively.

8
00:00:18,674 --> 00:00:20,085
As the project manager,

9
00:00:20,085 --> 00:00:21,600
you are the one who connects

10
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,285
your team to the
information they need.

11
00:00:24,285 --> 00:00:26,010
Throughout the project, you'll

12
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:27,600
serve as the main resource for

13
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,920
your team when it comes to

14
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:31,425
communicating and
clarifying goals,

15
00:00:31,425 --> 00:00:34,180
action items,
progress, and updates.

16
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,940
It's important to make sure that

17
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,680
you are carrying
information forward

18
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,850
consistently and coherently
so that everyone

19
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:42,350
understands what the
current state of

20
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:45,350
the project is and
what happens next.

21
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:48,710
Teams communicate in
a myriad of ways.

22
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:50,630
Though project managers
are constantly

23
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:52,805
communicating through
check-ins and meetings,

24
00:00:52,805 --> 00:00:54,320
project documents such as

25
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,285
project plans
including schedules,

26
00:00:56,285 --> 00:00:57,530
trackers, and meeting notes,

27
00:00:57,530 --> 00:01:00,430
they're also hubs for
team communication.

28
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,690
It's your responsibility
to be clear

29
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:05,030
about how those
documents get used,

30
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:07,145
who has access to
those documents,

31
00:01:07,145 --> 00:01:10,340
and how often the
documents get updated.

32
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,670
Of course, in addition to
those responsibilities,

33
00:01:13,670 --> 00:01:15,650
you'll also have to field e-mails,

34
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:17,870
instant messages,
and attend meetings.

35
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:19,400
All of these things are critical

36
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:21,035
in driving a project forward.

37
00:01:21,035 --> 00:01:22,340
As a project manager,

38
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:23,825
you are the one who coordinates

39
00:01:23,825 --> 00:01:26,330
incoming and outgoing
information.

40
00:01:26,330 --> 00:01:29,150
You connect individuals to
the necessary details and

41
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:31,400
context and track who

42
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,180
needs to receive what
information and when.

43
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:37,145
You'll need to communicate
certain information

44
00:01:37,145 --> 00:01:40,645
to your team multiple
times and in various ways.

45
00:01:40,645 --> 00:01:42,755
Some people learn by listening,

46
00:01:42,755 --> 00:01:44,375
some people learn by watching,

47
00:01:44,375 --> 00:01:46,280
and others learn by doing.

48
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:48,440
Communicating in various ways

49
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,390
ensures that you're
sharing knowledge to

50
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:52,070
your team in a format that's

51
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:55,030
digestible and easy
for them to take in.

52
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:58,655
Your team will have a lot
of tasks to focus on.

53
00:01:58,655 --> 00:02:00,650
Be proactive and reinforce

54
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,795
important information
multiple times,

55
00:02:02,795 --> 00:02:06,160
in multiple ways so that no
one is left out of the loop.

56
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,460
There are many tools for

57
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,770
communicating with your
team to make it easy to

58
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:11,240
keep in contact and be on

59
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:13,820
the same page throughout the
duration of the project.

60
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,504
Some of these include:
e-mail and messaging,

61
00:02:16,504 --> 00:02:19,190
in-person meetings,
video conferencing,

62
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:21,730
and work management and
collaboration tools.

63
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:23,300
Your organization might have

64
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:25,295
some of these tools
in place already,

65
00:02:25,295 --> 00:02:26,960
or you might have
the opportunity to

66
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,120
select some for a project.

67
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,220
In either case, it's good to be

68
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,990
familiar with what's out there.

69
00:02:32,990 --> 00:02:34,850
We'll explore tools that provide

70
00:02:34,850 --> 00:02:37,040
effective project
team communication in

71
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:41,150
more detail in the next
video. Meet you there.
